      ":question/id": "2dd924e4-dd60-54b1-9a1e-93f6380c91b5",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $4^{x-3}=7$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take $\\log_4$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4^{x-3}&=7\\\\\n\\log_4\\left(4^{x-3}\\right)&=\\log_4(7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ gives $x-3=\\log_4(7)$. Adding $3$ to both sides, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=\\log_4(7)+3.\n$$"
    }
